        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "optical",
        "summary": "Nd8 shows NIR Nd3+ emission at 927, 1078, 1360, and 1843 nm. Quantum efficiency of the 4F3/2 → 4I11/2 transition is 16 ± 0.2% (highest reported for a molecular Nd compound in this paper), with stimulated emission cross section 3.04 × 10−20 cm2. Fluorescence lifetime 186 ± 0.9 μs (1078 nm) and 78 ± 0.4 μs (927 nm); radiative lifetime 1187 μs. Red-shifted bands versus Nd1 attributed to greater covalency/nephelauxetic effect. Energy-transfer quenching is dipole–dipole (critical separation ~1 nm) with later-time migration.",
